      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When you ship furniture from Bhubaneswar to Kolkata, every step of the journey is governed by specific statutory paperwork and risk coverage. The first requirement is the <strong>GST e‑Way bill</strong>, a digital permit that must be generated before any goods leave the state.</p>
<p>Next, the freight operator must secure an <strong>IBA‑approved Lorry Receipt (LR/Bilty)</strong> which records the cargo details, consignor and consignee information, and the route. These documents together ensure compliance with Indian customs and tax regulations.</p>

<h3>Risk Coverage: Marine Transit Insurance</h3>
<p>To protect your valuable items against accidental collision, fire, or unforeseen delays, you should opt for a <strong>100 % declared‑value IRDAI marine transit insurance</strong>. This policy covers the entire transit route, offering peace of mind that any damage or loss will be compensated at full declared value.</p>
<p>It is especially important for high‑value furniture that may be exposed to rough handling or weather conditions during road transport.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">When planning the move, you’ll also need to consider the <strong>packers and movers costs from Kolkata to Bhubaneswar</strong> and vice versa.</p>
